{
	"note": [
		"RM-004 B4 pixel oracle: the same geometry, camera and sampler state rendered",
		"once with the authored texture and once with the resized one, differenced in",
		"the framebuffer. This is the only measurement in the sprint that looks at what",
		"a user sees rather than at what the files contain.",
		"",
		"Run once, from a scaffold under public/_oracle/ that is NOT committed - it",
		"needs the pre-resize originals, which are 4.13 MB and live in git history.",
		"The permanent protection is the cap test and the gates in tests/texture-resize",
		".test.js; this file is the evidence behind the choice of 1024, kept so the",
		"decision can be revisited without re-deriving it. To reproduce: restore the",
		"originals with git show <pre-B4>:public/<path>, serve them beside the shipped",
		"files, and render both.",
		"",
		"Columns, all rms in 0-255 units over a full frame:",
		"  self        the same file loaded twice. 0.00 everywhere, which is what makes",
		"              the rest of the table trustworthy.",
		"  codec       the original re-encoded at its ORIGINAL size at q95. Generation",
		"              loss that would be there with no resize at all.",
		"  total       the shipped resize.",
		"  resolution  sqrt(total^2 - codec^2): the part attributable to resolution, and",
		"              the only part a different cap would change.",
		"",
		"READ THE CURVE, NOT THE WORST NUMBER. For each texture the difference stays",
		"roughly flat while the display is smaller than the RESIZED texture, then jumps",
		"once the display exceeds it and the GPU starts magnifying. Below that point",
		"the resized file still carries at least one texel per screen pixel, so the",
		"difference is mip-chain alignment rather than missing information - and at",
		"669x1024 the resized wood is at 1:1 and therefore SHARPER than the original",
		"being minified to the same size. Above it the loss is real.",
		"",
		"Honest summary: Ground_4K (<=1.43 at every size, and tiled x40 by skybox.js)",
		"and white_wood (<=1.24) are free. Garden is free to 512px and reaches 8.30 at",
		"its native 2048 - a size the sky dome never samples at, since it spreads the",
		"panorama across a FOV that already magnifies it. The two dark woods carry a",
		"real 2.3-3.7 difference at realistic sizes, worst pixels 23-39/255. That is",
		"small, measurable, and not nothing: it is what 52.56 MB of the 61.67 MB saved",
		"actually cost."
	],
